1
00:00:00,600 --> 00:00:14,270
-crf 0: lossless in one AV1 encoder.

2
00:00:14,270 --> 00:00:22,080
Not in the other.

3
00:00:22,080 --> 00:00:30,340
libaom -crf 0: SSIM 1, PSNR infinite.

4
00:00:30,340 --> 00:00:36,240
Decoded frames equal the source.

5
00:00:36,240 --> 00:00:45,570
SVT -crf 0 = no -crf. Log: CRF 35.

6
00:00:45,570 --> 00:00:50,750
SSIM 0.9885 on 8.1.2. Lossy.

7
00:00:50,750 --> 00:01:00,240
-crf 30: SVT 61 kB, then 82 kB.

8
00:01:00,240 --> 00:01:07,350
libaom 41 kB on both builds.

9
00:01:07,350 --> 00:01:16,440
-b:v 0 next to -crf: nothing changes.

10
00:01:16,440 --> 00:01:21,630
Both encoders, both builds.

11
00:01:21,630 --> 00:01:30,820
libaom obeys -b:v: 512 kB to 223 kB.

12
00:01:30,820 --> 00:01:38,860
SVT: ignored on 6.1.1, error on 8.1.2.

13
00:01:38,860 --> 00:01:44,550
SVT preset 12: 55% bigger than 8.

14
00:01:44,550 --> 00:01:49,420
And worse: SSIM 0.99 vs 0.997.

15
00:01:49,420 --> 00:01:55,370
SVT: keyframes at 0, 161, 322.

16
00:01:55,370 --> 00:02:02,320
libaom: 0 only. -g 25: 16 each.

17
00:02:02,320 --> 00:02:11,800
Frame 300: SVT 140, libaom 301.

18
00:02:11,800 --> 00:02:19,700
With -g 25: 1 frame.

19
00:02:19,700 --> 00:02:27,150
Measured on ffmpeg 6.1.1 and 8.1.2.

20
00:02:27,150 --> 00:02:33,360
Not tested: real footage, players.
